{"t":1792719028,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"0864ecd3-69af-486d-a48b-70523ce2dd3e","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-23T00:46:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 230046\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n846 PM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nNo changes needed. Coastal flooding advisories remain in effect\nfor many locations. Check the latest CFW for updates. Also, see\nthe marine forecast discussion below for details about the small\ncraft advisories into Friday.\n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Dry and seasonable conditions continue through early next\n  week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and seasonable conditions continue through \nearly next week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\nSurface high pressure remains to the north through Saturday with\ndry and seasonable conditions expected to continue. Tonight's\nlow temperatures will be in the upper 30s to 40s. For Friday \nand Saturday, surface high pressure extends southward from \nCanada with dry cold fronts bringing in cooler air. High \ntemperatures stay in the 50s to low 60s while overnight lows \nplummet into the 30s for most. The exception will be east of the\nI-95 corridor where low temperatures stay in the low 40s. Frost\nis possible Friday night and Saturday night. \n\nHigh pressure will continue to build southward into the region \nSunday through Tuesday. Dry conditions and seasonable \ntemperatures expected each day with light north to east winds. A\nbackdoor cold front could try to push into the region Tuesday \ninto Tuesday night, but will have very little to no moisture \nwith it to produce any precipitation. A surge of cooler \ntemperatures will follow behind the front for the day on \nWednesday.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /00Z FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nWinds become light overnight before shifting to northeast on \nFriday. Winds blow 5 to 10 knots on Friday before becoming light\nand variable overnight. On Saturday, winds shift to easterly, \nremaining light throughout the day. VFR conditions are expected \neach day. \n\nVFR conditions Sunday through Monday night. Winds light and variable \nthrough the period as high pressure sits overhead. Winds then\nturn out of the NNE on Tuesday AOB 10 knots for the most part.\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nSmall Craft Advisory conditions continue across the Chesapeake\nBay and lower tidal potomac overnight into Friday. Winds will \ndiminish in the northern Bay, but the middle Chesapeake Bay \nwaters will likely remain elevated at least for a portion of the\nafternoon. \n\nFriday evening through Saturday, light winds are expected \nacross the waters. The exception will be in the southern \nportions of the Chesapeake Bay where wind gusts near advisory \ncriteria, so that SCA may need to be extended in time. \n\nLight winds expected Sunday and Monday with high pressure\noverhead. However, by Tuesday winds will turn out of the NNE \nand increase a bit. It is possible that winds could approach SCA\ncriteria in channeling flow along the Chesapeake Bay.\n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\nElevated tide levels are expected through the weekend as we approach \nthe Full Moon on October 26, along with being in King Tide season \n(though we are already past the highest astronomical tides that were \nat the beginning of October). Sensitive locations are forecast to \nreach Action Stage during most of the high tide cycles this week, \nwith Annapolis, Solomons Island, Dahlgren, Straits Point, and \nAlexandria expected to reach minor over the next few cycles.\nNumerous Coastal Flood Advisories remain in effect for these\nareas, with extensions possible in some locations. The presence\nof northerly winds is likely to keep tidal flooding within \nMinor flood stage.\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Small Craft Advisory until 11 AM EDT Friday for MDZ008.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory until 7 PM EDT Friday for MDZ014.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory until 3 AM EDT Friday for MDZ016-018.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory until 3 AM EDT Friday for MDZ017.\nVA...Coastal Flood Advisory until 3 AM EDT Friday for VAZ057.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory until 11 AM EDT Friday for ANZ530>532-\n     538>540.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 6 PM EDT Friday for ANZ533-534-537-\n     541>543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...AVS/KLW/CJL\nAVIATION...AVS/KLW/CJL\nMARINE...AVS/KLW/CJL\n"},"forecast":{"t":1792718979,"days":{"2026-10-22":{"hi":null,"lo":46,"pop":0,"short":"Clear"},"2026-10-23":{"hi":64,"lo":40,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-24":{"hi":64,"lo":42,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-25":{"hi":67,"lo":43,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-26":{"hi":70,"lo":50,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-27":{"hi":69,"lo":48,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-28":{"hi":65,"lo":50,"pop":3,"short":"Partly Sunny"},"2026-10-29":{"hi":68,"lo":null,"pop":6,"short":"Mostly Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1792717200,"n":48,"ceil":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0],"spd":[5,5,5,5,5,6,6,6,7,7,6,6,7,8,8,8,7,7,7,6,6,5,4,4,3,3,3,2,2,1,1,1,2,2,2,3,3,3,4,4,4,4,4,3,3,3,2,2],"gst":[12,12,12,13,14,14,14,14,14,14,13,13,13,13,13,12,12,11,10,10,9,8,8,8,8,7,7,6,5,5,4,5,5,5,6,6,7,7,7,7,6,6,6,5,5,5,4,4],"dir":[340,350,350,0,0,10,10,10,10,20,20,30,30,40,40,40,40,30,40,40,40,40,40,50,70,80,90,90,80,80,80,60,50,50,50,40,50,60,60,70,80,80,80,70,70,70,80,80],"pop":[0,0,0,0,0,0,